    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X5GbEkTg1acJJLTffK42Xc)_\n\nAdds `sp-author-notes` (`M-x sp-author-notes`, `sp-author-notes-preview`), documented in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-author-notes.org`.\n\nWhat it does:\n- Reads `litnotes/` (file-level meta only) and fixes typos of `pub-author` (`pub-authro`, `Pub_Author`; two edits away is only reported).\n- Creates a `:person:` note for each plain author name with no note, via `sp-org--write-note`, and turns the name into an `[[id:...]]` link. (`sp-org--create-note` does not exist; this is the function behind `sp-org-create-note-and-link`.)\n- In each `:person:` author note: ensures `* Basics`, then `* Works` after it, then a `collection-query-table` block (`:parent-of \"self\" :parent-prop \"pub-author\"`, columns title, read-status, read-priority, pub-year, relevance-factor, sorted by pub-year) unless one exists.\n- Report buffer of fixed / created / converted / updated notes, plus things left alone.\n\nSafety: preview first, asks before writing; idempotent; insert-only; backups in `author-notes-backups/`; skips files with unsaved buffers; ambiguous or conflicting titles are reported, not touched.\n\nTested: 8 ERT tests in Emacs 29.3 batch with a temporary vault (`sp-org--write-note` stubbed). Not tested: the real `~/notes`, vulpea DB, filling the dblocks, the report buffer on screen.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAXf5syXqG5HjUbdK7)_",
